{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2021-04-06 11:00:00', 'title': 'S&P DOW JONES INDICES REPORTS U.S. INDICATED DIVIDEND PAYMENTS INCREASED $18.0 BILLION IN Q1 2021', 'text': "NEW YORK, APRIL 6, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0S&P DOW JONES INDICES ANNOUNCED TODAY THAT INDICATED DIVIDEND NET CHANGES (INCREASES LESS DECREASES) FOR U.S. DOMESTIC COMMON STOCKS INCREASED $18.0 BILLION DURING Q1 2021, COMPARED TO $9.5 BILLION IN Q4 2020, -$2.3 BILLION IN Q3 2020, -$42.5 BILLION IN Q2 2020, -$5.5 BILLION IN Q1 2020, AND A GAIN OF $10.6 BILLION IN Q4 2019. FOR Q1 2021, AGGREGATE INCREASES AMOUNTED TO $20.3 BILLION, THE LARGEST QUARTERLY INCREASE SINCE Q1 2012'S $26.1 BILLION, UP 46.9% FROM Q4 2020'S $13.9 BILLION, AND UP 63.7% FROM THE $12.4 BILLION INCREASE IN Q1 2020."}